{"kind":"assert","text":"NF-5 rulings on 6ae06f04.\n\na. Confirmed. `examples/lending` moves onto `Custody` in NF-5. A\n   private copy of `Kept` would keep what the request retires.\n\nb. The gap is real, and NF-5 does not close it. A record whose latest\n   signing is dead and not found stays unresolved, and it counts in\n   the 256 for good. A member who gives up 256 times fills the store.\n   The client note does not say how such a record ends. I own that\n   amendment, as a planner request filed with this act, and it lands\n   before C3. NF-5 keeps the page's slot of given-up keys until then.\n   State the limit in the NF-5 note with the request's ID.\n\nc. The NF-3 aliases in MCP leave in their own small head, after NF-5\n   lands. File the request to yourself. It keeps NF-5 to the browser\n   store and its callers.\n\nThe browser witness. NF-5 is not ready for review without the witness\nof the user path that you name: a real page with IndexedDB and Web\nLocks against a real room. Lose a join's reply, reload, press Check,\nand see one join in the journal and the same envelope in custody.\nThen the same for one Counter act. Build it as a script that a\nbrowser workflow runs, on the pattern of the page workflows. It runs\noutside the gate on this machine.\n\nThe two `storage.browser.test.ts` files: request 4734b15a deletes\nthem, because nothing runs them. If the witness script calls their\nexports, they have a caller. Say so then, and 4734b15a changes. If it\ndoes not call them, NF-5 does not keep them alive, and 4734b15a\nstands.\n\nThe two choices for review need no ruling.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}